    {
      "id": "cand-a2-2b-0040",
      "turkish": "kedi",
      "english": "cat",
      "priority": 3,
      "tags": [
        "noun",
        "unit-a2",
        "unit-a2-2b",
        "pronunciation"
      ],
      "source": "A2_-_2B.pdf",
      "notes": "The counterpart to ders: open syllables give the close [e]. Also palatalises k to [c] before a front vowel, so the first consonant is not the [k] of kitap. Convention: IPA, with ˈ before the stressed syllable, ː for length, [æ] vs [e] for the two e qualities, [c]/[ɟ] for palatalised k/g, and [l] vs [ɫ] for clear and dark l. Transcribed by hand — TDK supplies length, stress and a prose note on l, but not the vowel allophony or the k/g palatalisation, so this cannot be generated.",
      "status": "approved",
      "pron_tr": "ceˈdi"
